=== file: README.md ===
# Article five-point support check

This Loom workflow creates exactly five concise summary points from an article, then independently checks every point against the article. If points are unsupported, it revises and rechecks the summary for at most two attempts. Any unsupported point after the second attempt is routed to a human reviewer. Invalid checker output is also routed to human review. If summary generation cannot continue, the workflow reports that verification is incomplete.

The summarizer and checker have separate prompt files in `prompts/`. Neither agent has tools. The checker treats the article as data, and its structured output is validated before the workflow reads it.

## Run and validate

From this project directory:

```text
weave check main.loom --no-env
weave test main.loom
weave eval main.loom --mock
```

No tool credentials or external services are configured by this project. Run with the model provider configured for `gpt-6-luna`.

## Human review

The workflow asks the reviewer to examine the article, current five-point summary, checker evidence, and reason for escalation. The returned result remains `HUMAN_REVIEW`; human input does not turn the summary into a model-verified result.

## Changing the workflow

Keep the summary at exactly five points and keep checker answers structured. Update `tests/main.test.yaml` when changing branches or the two-attempt limit, and update the relevant golden dataset when changing an agent's expected behavior.
=== end ===
